d  I have contracted it obviously Boris  Johnson did so you know do we have a  smoking gun here that something is awry  no should we expect that something will  happen tomorrow probably not but again I  want to emphasize because of the focus  on coven 19 which is totally appropriate  and all the things that means we haven't  been thinking about North Korea but at  North Korea if the leader dies in a  context in which there's a global  pandemic it's under sanctions and  entering a recession as China's economy  declines that's a big deal and we might  want to think about that before it  happens rather than after it happens  sure Jim we've talked now a little bit  about Kim Jones health so let me ask you  what is the state of North Korea's  health system what sort of treatment  could Kim jong-un expect in country well  I think it's mixed obviously he's gonna  get the best health care of anyone in  that country bar none and you know there  are as you referenced reports the  Chinese doctors have made their way but  the health care system in general is not  very good and in terms of public health  and so you know that there are a lot of  unknowns here and we don't know what  coronavirus is doing in North Korea but  if it did manage to enter that public  health system is not prepared to deal  with that and I've had reports from the  ground that suggests that because the  North Koreans are essentially shutting  everything down there really aren't a  lot of international doctors  international medical aid workers in  North Korea to help with that and so you  know they're what 15 Europeans another  dozen UN officials not a lot of folks to  help the North Koreans deal with this so  you know whether it's its own health  problems maybe he has no health problems  at all but I think this bears watching  because it could lead to economic and  social instability in the country that  doesn't have nuclear weapons and feels  like we're threatening them so maybe we  should pay attention